<title>USA: Wang sees charge from deal, quarter loss.</title>
<headline>Wang sees charge from deal, quarter loss.</headline>
<dateline>BILLERICA, Mass. 1996-08-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Wang Laboratories Inc said Friday it will take an unspecified charge in the current first quarter due to the acquisition of I-NET Inc and will report a net loss for the quarter.</p>
<p>Wang said it completed the $167 million acquisition of I-NET, a Bethesda, Md.-based network and desktop outsourcing company. I-NET posted 1995 revenues of $327 million.</p>
<p>Wang previously said it expected the deal to be dilutive during fiscal 1997, but accretive thereafter.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212-859-1610</p>
